      "navLabel": "",
      "heading": "Before and at Albion",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "parts": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Birmingham-born Moore was a centre-back and Jamaica international. He joined Albion in September 2001 and helped win promotions in 2002 and 2004, before playing his part in the 2005 Great Escape."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "label": "Albion: Darren Moore in profile, 18 May 2018",
          "url": "https://www.wba.co.uk/news/2018/may/darren-moore-in-profile"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text-panel",
      "anchor": "chapter-2",
      "navLabel": "",
      "heading": "The Albion story",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "parts": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "He returned to the club as an academy coach after retiring as a player. His six-match interim spell in 2018 brought wins over Manchester United, Newcastle and Tottenham, but could not prevent relegation."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
        {
          "label": "Albion: Darren Moore in profile, 18 May 2018",
          "url": "https://www.wba.co.uk/news/2018/may/darren-moore-in-profile"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text-panel",
      "anchor": "chapter-3",
      "navLabel": "",
      "heading": "The next chapter",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "parts": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Appointed permanent head coach on 18 May 2018, he left after the Ipswich draw on 9 March 2019. The caretaker and permanent periods are recorded separately here."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sources": [
